          "blocks": {
            "intro_text": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Beef tenderloin is a special-occasion roast, and it's also one of the easiest to overcook. It's lean, so there's very little fat to cover a mistake, and a few degrees is the difference between a perfect medium rare and a gray band of overcooked meat.</p><p>That's why Chris usually cooks it sous vide. But you don't need a water bath to get the same result. Roast it in a very low oven, watch the temperature inside the meat instead of the clock, and sear it at the end.</p>",
