            "why_1_p": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>The oven dial isn't the temperature your roast is cooking at. The real cooking temperature is the surface of the meat. Start the oven hot, turn it way down as the surface nears your target, then wait for the core to catch up. You get an edge-to-edge roast, just like you'd expect from sous vide, with no gray ring of overcooked meat under the crust.</p>",
