                "recipe_sub_1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p><strong>Red wine sauce</strong></p><p>This is Chris's take on Marco Pierre White's red wine sauce, made quick because the demi-glace has already done the hard work. The one rule is that the wine has to be good enough to drink.</p><p><strong>Makes</strong> about 270g, enough for a whole roast (6 to 8 servings)<br><strong>Prep</strong> 10 minutes<br><strong>Cook</strong> 45 minutes to 1 hour</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "recipe_note": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Recipes by Chris Young.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "0.875rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color8 }}",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "recipe_method": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p><strong>Serves</strong> 4 to 6<br><strong>Prep</strong> 10 to 15 minutes<br><strong>Cook</strong> low and slow, the countdown tells you when</p><ol><li><strong>Truss and season.</strong> Use butcher's twine to truss the tenderloin in three spots, creating four even sections. Season with 1% of its weight in salt.</li><li><strong>Preheat the oven</strong> to 400°F (205°C).</li><li><strong>Insert the thermometer.</strong> Insert the Combustion Predictive Thermometer into the thickest part of the roast, past the minimum insertion line. Set it for 129°F (54°C) for medium rare.</li><li><strong>Start hot.</strong> Roast on a rack and watch the surface temperature. It takes a while for the surface to come up from fridge temperature.</li><li><strong>Turn the oven down.</strong> As the surface temperature gets close to 129°F (54°C), turn the oven down to about 225°F (107°C) so the surface doesn't overshoot.</li><li><strong>Wait for the core to catch up.</strong> Leave it until the core temperature comes up to the surface temperature. The countdown tells you when.</li><li><strong>Sear.</strong> Just before you're ready to serve, put the roast back into a hot oven for 4 or 5 minutes to crisp up the surface.</li><li><strong>Slice and serve</strong> with the red wine sauce (below).</li></ol>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {},
                  "name": "Method"
                },
                "sauce_anchor": {
                  "type": "custom-liquid",
                  "name": "Anchor #tl-sauce",
                  "settings": {
                    "custom_liquid": "<div id=\"tl-sauce\"></div>"
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "sauce_ingr_h": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<h3>Ingredients</h3>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
                    "font_size": "0.75rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "loose",
                    "case": "uppercase",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color8 }}",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "sauce_ingr": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<ul><li>51g clarified butter (¼ cup)</li><li>225g shallots (about 6), thinly sliced</li><li>3 garlic cloves, split</li><li>48g red wine vinegar (3 tbsp)</li><li>102g port (about 7 tbsp), plus more to taste</li><li>750ml red wine (one bottle, about 3¼ cups)</li><li>9.6g tomato paste (a generous 1½ tsp), or 32g passata (2 tbsp)</li><li>201g veal demi-glace (a generous ¾ cup), from the stock recipe</li><li>2 or 3 small sprigs parsley</li><li>2 or 3 small sprigs tarragon</li><li>Salt and MSG, to taste</li><li>A few knobs of cold unsalted butter</li></ul><p>For 2 or 3 people, make a third of the recipe (250ml of wine).</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "sauce_method_h": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<h3>Method</h3>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "custom",
                    "font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
                    "font_size": "0.75rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "loose",
                    "case": "uppercase",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color8 }}",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "sauce_method": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<ol><li><strong>Sweat the shallots.</strong> Melt the clarified butter in a medium saucepan and sweat the shallots and garlic until soft and lightly caramelized.</li><li><strong>Cook off the vinegar.</strong> Add the vinegar and cook it down until the pot is nearly dry.</li><li><strong>Add wine and port, then flame.</strong> Add the port and red wine, bring to a simmer and carefully ignite to burn off the alcohol (hood fan off, lid within reach).</li><li><strong>Reduce to syrup.</strong> Reduce the wine and port all the way down until syrupy, before the demi-glace goes in.</li><li><strong>Add demi and herbs.</strong> Stir in the tomato paste (or passata) and demi-glace, add the parsley and tarragon, and bring back to a simmer. Reduce until it just coats the back of a spoon. Don't take it further.</li><li><strong>Strain and finish.</strong> Strain through a fine sieve, season with salt and MSG to taste, and swirl in the cold butter until glossy.</li></ol><p>It keeps covered in the fridge, and any extra freezes well. The demi-glace comes from Chris's 15-Minute Veal Stock recipe.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color7 }}",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {},
                  "name": "Sauce method"
                }
